    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current Pollution Under Control (PUC) Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid PUC certifies that the car meets environmental standards. Transporters in India require this to avoid fines during transit.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The insurance policy should cover the vehicle for the entire journey, including roadside assistance. It protects against accidental damage and theft.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The International Bargaining Association (IBA) consignment bilty is a standard transport document that details the cargo, its value, and the route. This bilty must be signed by the consignor and the carrier.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Each document must be current, legible, and in the original format or a certified copy. Transport companies often require you to submit scanned copies in advance, so keep digital backups handy.</p>

<h3>Why 100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance Matters</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">While the standard insurance covers basic risks, a <strong>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong> offers full coverage for the vehicle’s actual market value.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This type of policy ensures that if the car is damaged, stolen, or suffers any loss during the sea or rail segment of the journey, you receive compensation equal to its full value, not a capped amount.</span></li></ul>

<p>Choosing this insurance is especially prudent for high‑value cars or luxury models. It eliminates the uncertainty of partial payouts and protects your investment throughout the entire transport chain, from Noida to Mumbai and beyond.</p>

<p>In summary, keep your self‑attested RC, valid PUC, insurance certificate, and IBA consignment bilty ready. Pair them with a 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance policy, and your car transport will be documented, insured, and ready for a hassle‑free journey.</p></div>
