</div>
	<h3>Odometer Verification</h3>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare the vehicle's odometer reading with the information provided on the Landing Document (LR Bill of Lading)</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If the odometer reading is different from the information on the LR Bill of Lading, discuss this discrepancy with the receiving party and attempt to reach a mutual agreement</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If a discrepancy is found, document the issue and ensure both parties sign off on the LR Bill of Lading, highlighting the odometer verification process</span></li>
	</ul>
	<h3>Signed Condition Sign-off</h3>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Review the condition of the vehicle with the receiving party and ensure they have a clear understanding of the vehicle's condition</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Ask the receiving party to sign off on the LR Bill of Lading, acknowledging their acceptance of the vehicle's condition</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Ensure that all damages, if any, are documented on the LR Bill of Lading and both parties sign and date the document</span></li>
	</ul>
	<p>After completing the above tasks, the vehicle is deemed in satisfactory condition and can be handed over to the receiving party.</p>
	<p>During the daylight condition re-inspection, it is crucial to ensure that the vehicle matches the state it was in when picked up.</p>
	<p>When verifying the odometer reading, compare it with the information provided in the LR Bill of Lading to confirm the vehicle's mileage is accurate.</p>
	<p>Before the vehicle is handed over, it is essential to ensure the receiving party acknowledges and accepts the vehicle's condition by signing and dating the LR Bill of Lading.</p>
	<p>In case any damages are identified during the re-inspection, the LR Bill of Lading should be amended to reflect the new condition and both parties should sign and date the updated document.</p>
	<p>By thoroughly reviewing the vehicle's condition, verifying the odometer reading, and ensuring a signed LR Bill of Lading, both parties can be confident in the vehicle's condition and avoid disputes later on.</p></div>
